WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.369 --> 00:00:04.650
CHANDA: On August 7th last year

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.520
Mrs. Benazir Bhutto

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.369
came to Yale University and sat down with me 
at this studio

00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:12.959
to discuss the state of affairs in her country.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:15.879
She told me why she wanted to go back home.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:16.900
She said

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.760
it was not for herself

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.579
but to save,

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:21.730
as she put it,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.740
"Save my country from

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.909
destruction and

00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:29.820
disintegration."

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.370
On December 27th last year

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.770
she was assassinated just after she had delivered
a speech

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.210
condemning extremism.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.850
In the interview she gave to me

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.050
on August 7th last year,

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:45.940
she said

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.760
"We want an end to the attacks on NATO and Afghan forces

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.810
in nearby Afghanistan by the militants

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.170
and we want an end to the

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:54.980
militants

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.900
who try to hijack our foreign policy by conducting
attacks on the Indian parliament

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.780
and on other sites in India.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.570
So our world-vision

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.380
collides rather dramatically with the world-vision
of the extremists."

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:14.380
How true she was.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.550
We are pleased to have in our studios
Mrs. Benazir Bhutto,

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.580
two-time prime minister of Pakistan,

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.440
and we are extremely pleased to have her

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.820
with us today

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.360
at a time

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.040
when Pakistan is facing

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.299
a critical

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:30.980
choice

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.040
about its future.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:33.939
Welcome, Mrs. Bhutto.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:39.390
BHUTTO: Thank you, Mr. Nanda [Chanda]. It's lovely to be at Yale.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.680
CHANDA: Thank you. Politics is as far removed 
from poetry as possible

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.290
so I cannot resist

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.370
reading a little poem that you wrote

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.230
some years ago.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.409
"One has might,

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.920
The other, right.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.710
One has the sword,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.840
The other, the pen.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.500
Guns rust and fall apart,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.840
Ideas live forever."

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.799
So do you think President Musharraf's guns are rusting

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:07.530
and that is why he's turning to you to do a deal?

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.959
BHUTTO: Certainly, there has been a degree of unease

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:14.549
within Pakistan. General Musharraf

00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:16.949
had given a charter of where he wanted to take the country

00:02:16.949 --> 00:02:21.439
which was towards a true democracy and a
moderate society.

00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:23.719
However, in the last six years,

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:28.790
we've seen that the extremists have spread
throughout the country, and we used to think

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.849
it was just

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:35.719
in the tribal areas, but indeed the Red Mosque
Incident in our capital city of Islamabad

00:02:35.719 --> 00:02:39.129
showed that the tentacles of extremism
were spreading

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.419
and that poses grave challenges to 
Pakistan from within,

00:02:43.419 --> 00:02:46.819
as well as complicates the external picture.

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:48.920
CHANDA: So the reason why he is

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.489
now willing to

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:52.040
sit down with you

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.450
is because he's

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.469
feeling that he's no longer in

00:02:55.469 --> 00:02:56.930
full control?

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:02.379
BHUTTO: I see it differently. I think after 9/11,
when the first general elections were held

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:03.510
under General Musharraf,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.579
it was less than a year later,

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:11.169
and he was seen very much as a strong ally
of the West on which the international

00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:12.699
community could depend

00:03:12.699 --> 00:03:14.939
to reform the madrasahs

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:19.650
and to constrain and restrain the terrorist
elements within the country.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.989
But unfortunately, since then,

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:24.809
there has been the rise of suicide bombings.

00:03:24.809 --> 00:03:28.199
Innocent people in Pakistan, like our women and children,

00:03:28.199 --> 00:03:29.669
are being killed,

00:03:29.669 --> 00:03:35.459
and I think now the international community
has started supporting the democratic process.

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:38.659
Within Pakistan we've had a pro-democracy
movement

00:03:38.659 --> 00:03:43.869
which has gathered strength as poverty in
the country increased and people's needs were neglected.

00:03:43.869 --> 00:03:49.590
So this confluence has made the
elections of 2007 very important.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.979
All the independent polls show that the
Pakistan People's Party and I

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:55.779
would go on to win any fair

00:03:55.779 --> 00:03:57.010
election.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:01.169
So I think that this is what is the need
of drawing people together.

00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:06.170
In Pakistan we have different fault lines: 
we have one on dictatorship versus

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:06.919
democracy,

00:04:06.919 --> 00:04:08.499
and we have a second one

00:04:08.499 --> 00:04:13.189
on moderation versus fundamentalism
or extremism.

00:04:13.189 --> 00:04:16.769
So I think that General Musharraf is trying to
seek a way

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:23.020
out by having these contacts with the Pakistan
People's Party.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:26.959
CHANDA: Nawaz Sharif has suggested that

00:04:26.959 --> 00:04:29.169
one should do everything

00:04:29.169 --> 00:04:31.989
to remove the military from politics,

00:04:31.989 --> 00:04:33.049
and what

00:04:33.049 --> 00:04:33.929
you may be

00:04:33.929 --> 00:04:35.610
trying to do

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.729
would be seen by people as prolonging the
military rule rather than

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:41.190
getting rid of the military altogether.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.879
BHUTTO: I know that is what Mr. Nawaz Sharif is saying,
but I don't agree,

00:04:44.879 --> 00:04:49.109
and I find it very strange that Mr. Nawaz Sharif
talked to General Musharraf and got out

00:04:49.109 --> 00:04:50.449
in the year 2000,

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:52.020
which did prolong

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.610
military rule in my country.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:58.460
I was also offered that if I quit politics
for ten years, all the charges against me would

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.500
be dropped

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.879
and my husband would be released, but I refused

00:05:02.879 --> 00:05:03.960
that offer

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.009
because I felt that it would prolong

00:05:06.009 --> 00:05:07.800
military rule in my country,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.899
and now I'm talking because this is about
getting the

00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:11.790
uniform

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.930
out of the office of the presidency.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:17.299
This is about facilitating the transfer
to democracy,

00:05:17.299 --> 00:05:21.030
and as I said, we're talking, but we're not
there yet.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.069
So

00:05:22.069 --> 00:05:25.029
I'm really not in a position to tell
you today

00:05:25.029 --> 00:05:26.620
that there really will be

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.309
an agreement on the facilitated transfer
to democracy,

00:05:30.309 --> 00:05:31.960
but I do know one thing:

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:35.849
that a facilitated transfer to democracy is far
more preferable

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:38.669
than a situation of chaos on the streets

00:05:38.669 --> 00:05:41.409
that can be taken advantage of

00:05:41.409 --> 00:05:44.039
by extremist elements.

00:05:44.039 --> 00:05:50.349
So as a Pakistani leader who wants to
see the stability and the unity of my country

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:53.050
and see Pakistan go on the path of moderation,

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:56.320
I think it's important for me to explore

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.559
peaceful political options

00:05:58.559 --> 00:06:00.550
of a transfer to democracy.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:06.039
I will point out to you that no one believed
when the Shah of Iran was facing street riots

00:06:06.039 --> 00:06:07.789
that it would end up

00:06:07.789 --> 00:06:11.059
in an ayatollah revolution, but that's what
happened.

00:06:11.059 --> 00:06:14.949
And when the Mensheviks took to the streets in Russia,

00:06:14.949 --> 00:06:17.439
no one expected the Bolsheviks.

00:06:17.439 --> 00:06:22.050
So, you know, when we have a situation where
we have militants who are armed,

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:24.830
and we have political parties who are unarmed,

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.449
I would do my best

00:06:27.449 --> 00:06:29.509
to have a peaceful transfer,

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:32.599
but if that fails, maybe I won't be able to
stop

00:06:32.599 --> 00:06:34.409
the street agitation

00:06:34.409 --> 00:06:36.869
and that would be dangerous, so let's hope

00:06:36.869 --> 00:06:40.940
that we can indeed get, either through the
negotiations we are having

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.569
or through the Supreme Court of Pakistan,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.539
some kind of a

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:47.620
facilitated and

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:48.749
peaceful

00:06:48.749 --> 00:06:50.749
revival of the constitution,

00:06:50.749 --> 00:06:53.089
restoration of the democratic process,

00:06:53.089 --> 00:06:56.520
and a redress of people's social and economic
needs

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.770
so that terrorism and militancy

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.259
can be undermined.

00:07:01.259 --> 00:07:07.389
CHANDA: According to some press reports, the agreement
that has been reached between you and President Musharraf

00:07:07.389 --> 00:07:09.520
is that

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:14.179
he will be a civilian president while you'll be--

00:07:14.179 --> 00:07:18.080
a civilian president who'll be in charge of national
security and foreign affairs,

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.229
and you will be

00:07:19.229 --> 00:07:22.120
chief executive,

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:22.860
and

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.520
the ban on you

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.340
as running for prime minister for the third time

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.129
would be lifted and your family can return.

00:07:30.129 --> 00:07:30.930
Is there

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.639
any truth in this?

00:07:32.639 --> 00:07:35.709
BHUTTO: These are certainly some of the issues that
are being discussed.

00:07:35.709 --> 00:07:37.789
General Musharraf

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:41.459
wants to get elected from the present assemblies.
He thinks that's legal.

00:07:41.459 --> 00:07:45.699
We in the PPP believe that it's not legal,
so this matter is going to be decided really

00:07:45.699 --> 00:07:46.749
by the courts

00:07:46.749 --> 00:07:47.860
and perhaps by

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.080
public pressure too,

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.359
but ultimately it's a decision of

00:07:53.359 --> 00:07:54.829
legal dispute.

00:07:54.829 --> 00:07:58.649
The elections are going to be held later this
year. My concern is that those elections

00:07:58.649 --> 00:08:00.460
should be fair, free, and impartial.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.979
I believe what the
international crisis

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:04.629
group

00:08:04.629 --> 00:08:08.329
that military intervention in the country
is creating failed state

00:08:08.329 --> 00:08:12.759
which poses a danger to Pakistan's own security
as well as regional

00:08:12.759 --> 00:08:16.209
security. So I'd like those elections to be fair,

00:08:16.209 --> 00:08:20.620
and I think any attempt by General Musharraf
to manipulate those elections

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.509
will lead to a far bigger internal crisis
with far-reaching

00:08:24.509 --> 00:08:27.019
repercussions.

00:08:27.019 --> 00:08:31.669
We haven't reached an agreement yet because
everything the regime says it will do

00:08:31.669 --> 00:08:36.030
is post-presidential, -prime ministerial, and
-parliamentary elections

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.220
and my party doesn't want to be lead up the garden path.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:43.870
So we believe that the cooperation needs
to be calibrated

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.470
so that there are different phases

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.540
of implementation--

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.440
CHANDA: So, is it possible that

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:53.080
if he

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:56.250
gets re-elected by the parliament one more time,

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.350
but he

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.629
makes you the interim Prime Minister so
that

00:09:00.629 --> 00:09:02.630
there can be free and fair election

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.550
in December,

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:07.800
would you accept that?
BHUTTO: No, no no no. I'm not looking at this for myself.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.190
I'm looking at this for the empowerment
of my people,

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.540
and I'm looking at this for saving my country

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:18.000
from a militant takeover or, God forbid,

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.770
disintegration. I think it's the worst crisis
that we've faced

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.660
since 1971.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.630
What we are looking for

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:25.290
is

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.150
a cooperation once the uniform is off.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.900
The PPP cannot cooperate with a uniform presidency

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.330
which blurs the distinction

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:35.390
between civil and

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:36.900
military rule.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.890
Because the PPP has been fighting every single
military dictatorship that there has been

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.000
in the country

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.440
and we symbolize the aspirations of the people
for a democratic Pakistan.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.970
The PPP is also looking for the holding of
fair elections.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:53.130
We wouldn't like a situation where the elections
are manipulated

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.110
and then we are offered a handful of ministries

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.930
in return for legitimizing a fraudulent election.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:04.790
CHANDA: So what would be necessary for you to consider 
the election to be fair and free? What would be

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:10.710
the conditions? 
BHUTTO: Very good question, very good question. 
The all-parties conference held in July

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.260
earlier this year

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:17.620
which was hosted, which was called for, by the
Alliance for the Restoration of Democracy,

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.829
came up with the points that need to be implemented

00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:24.690
by the Election Commission of Pakistan
for the holding of fair elections,

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.100
and earlier,

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.220
the very widely-respected international
group

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:32.660
known as the NDI, the National Democratic Institute,

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:36.080
held a round table of all political parties
in Pakistan,

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:40.320
and the round table also came up with proposals,
and we have handed these proposals

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.040
over

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.690
to General Musharraf's side, and they have been promising
us for some months

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:49.280
that they will actually implement various proposals
that have come during the time

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:53.790
for fair elections, and they keep reassuring
us that the elections will be fair

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.999
but unfortunately, except for transparent
ballot boxes,

00:10:57.999 --> 00:11:00.470
none of those reforms have been implemented

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.579
which is really leading to some unease in the
PPP

00:11:03.579 --> 00:11:06.189
circles, and indeed the opposition circles,

00:11:06.189 --> 00:11:08.439
that now the elections are around the corner.

00:11:08.439 --> 00:11:11.909
When is this all going to happen? When are 
these reforms going to be

00:11:11.909 --> 00:11:12.730
lifted?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:16.680
Then there is also the issue of a balance
between the presidency and the parliament.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:20.480
I see little point in getting a parliament elected

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.930
where the prime minister is thrown out two 
months later.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.420
I mean, we had this in the 90's

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:29.130
where the presidential power to dismiss parliaments

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:33.379
was used ruthlessly, not only against Mr. Nawaz Sharif
and myself twice,

00:11:33.379 --> 00:11:35.389
but even against Mr. Junejo.

00:11:35.389 --> 00:11:39.809
So we feel that there is little point in taking
our country backwards to the instability of

00:11:39.809 --> 00:11:40.779
the 90's.

00:11:40.779 --> 00:11:44.200
We have to move forward towards a better political

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:48.100
system where we know what the role and responsibility
of the parliament is,

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.089
and what the role and responsibility

00:11:50.089 --> 00:11:55.050
of the president is. 
CHANDA: How does one reach that without a constitutional reform?

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:59.540
BHUTTO: Well, General Musharraf assures us that he wants
parliament to have all the powers,

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.310
and he says he doesn't want any powers himself,

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:06.850
but there's a dichotomy because the constitution
actually gives all the key powers

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:11.490
to the presidency. So this is an issue on which
the discussions are still ongoing,

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:15.440
because while General Musharraf says he wants all
powers to be with the parliament,

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:19.320
he seems unwilling to give up the presidential
power to dismiss

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:23.930
the parliament. So we are still having ongoing
discussions on that particular issue,

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:29.400
but we agree, both sides agree, that the
reform should be implemented for fair elections;

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:33.230
both sides agree that the ban on the twice-elected
prime minister should go;

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.860
both sides agree that the moderate forces should
come together;

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.630
both sides agree there should be a level playing field

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.970
and an end to moderated litigation.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:46.320
So there's a lot of agreement, apparent
agreement, on a lot of issues, while one

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.590
or two still

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.010
are outstanding,

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:53.170
but right now the issue is: when is the implementation
going to take place,

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:59.000
and then which phase is this implementation going
to take place? To complicate the issue,

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.440
the ruling party has been saying

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:06.139
that nothing will change and that they're
not really negotiating with the PPP

00:13:06.139 --> 00:13:09.120
they're just they're giving, in our local language:

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.160
"dheel"

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.290
That means a long rope.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.130
So this, and they keep talking about how they're
going to impose emergency.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:21.910
So some people have cynically remarked
that the Red Mosque Incident

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.990
in Islamabad was actually cooked up

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:29.210
by elements of the cabinet to provide
a pretext for emergency,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.800
but the plan failed

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:33.320
when the presidency decided

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.040
to take action

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.500
against the militants. So you know, we're talking
here about a country

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.220
from which many key Al-Qaeda

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.360
suspects have been,

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.430
or terrorists, have been arrested,

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:51.210
like Abu Zubaydah, and Khalid Sheikh from Pindi, 
and Ramzi Binalshibh

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.010
from Karachi.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:56.650
So we must remember that this is not just
a war for Pakistan's heart and soul;

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.890
this is something that will have far-reaching
ramifications

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:03.130
on militant struggles across our borders.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.950
We in the PPP are very determined

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.040
to build peace.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.900
In fact, we say the message of Islam
is peace,

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.860
and we want peace for our citizens inside our
country;

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:17.339
we want an end to the attacks on NATO and
Afghan troops in nearby Afghanistan,

00:14:17.339 --> 00:14:20.130
and we want an end to the militants who try to

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.710
hijack our foreign policy

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:26.430
by conducting attacks on the Indian parliament
or on other sites

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:27.690
in India.

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:30.970
So our world vision

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.780
collides rather dramatically

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:39.520
with the word vision of the extremists. Now
Musharraf has said he's for moderation,

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:42.570
and so we hope that he can do something
up front

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:46.160
that can facilitate moderate forces coming together.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:49.520
CHANDA: President Chaudhry Shujaat Hussain

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.920
of the Pakistan Muslim League has said that

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.210
maybe

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.950
there will be an imposition of emergency

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:00.570
and the assembly will be extended for one year.
If that happens,

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:02.230
then what will be the position of

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:03.340
your party?

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:07.700
BHUTTO: I believe my party would join with all
the other political parties

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.470
to protest any attempt to defer

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.860
the elections.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.940
What we have been telling

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.279
all of the other political parties-- we had
it all-parties conference in

00:15:18.279 --> 00:15:19.930
London

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:25.660
and we all agreed on certain points
for the holding of fair, free, and impartial elections,

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:30.480
but whereas the other political parties wanted
to start a movement straightaway,

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.650
we said, "No,

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:34.200
we have to wait.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.310
We have to wait and see whether either the elections
are postponed,

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:40.450
or we have to wait and see whether the elections
are rigged

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:43.430
but to start an agitation at this point

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:46.180
might tempt the rulers into

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:48.160
imposing emergency."

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.769
But I do think that if the doors of
election

00:15:50.769 --> 00:15:52.189
are shut on us

00:15:52.189 --> 00:15:54.190
and emergency is imposed

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:59.010
or the elections are rigged, then certainly
the PPP, with the other political parties,

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.430
civil groups, and NGOs

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.980
in Pakistan, would put pressure like in the Ukraine

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.240
during the Orange Revolution

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.220
for the empowerment of our people.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:14.550
CHANDA: So you can see a street protest of the type that

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.970
so recently involving the chief justice

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.500
perhaps a bigger

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:23.500
departisanization of political parties?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.450
BHUTTO: That's right, I very much can see that

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:30.910
happening. I wouldn't like to see it happening because
I don't think that Pakistan needs anarchy

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.630
or civil strife or bloodshed,

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.460
but both sides have a responsibility
to prevent that,

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.880
and the elections now

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.910
give General Musharraf and the presidency, as well as the military establishment,

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:47.420
an opportunity to take Pakistan safety

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.910
from one phase

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:51.810
of governance to another phase of governance.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:57.020
The spoilers are there. After all, why would those
who have politically benefited from

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:59.800
firing the shots from the shoulders of the
military

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:04.250
want to have fair elections which would
see them give up power

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:09.500
and go into opposition? So I understand that
there will be elements like the ruling PMLQ

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:13.329
which will do everything to scuttle a process
of reconciliation

00:17:13.329 --> 00:17:16.630
and resolution, moving Pakistan onto a moderate course,

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:20.800
but I think it's important for General Musharraf
and the military establishment

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.589
to stay the course,

00:17:22.589 --> 00:17:25.979
not to defer the elections, not to impose
emergency,

00:17:25.979 --> 00:17:29.330
and to make sure that those elections are credible

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:33.640
and satisfy the public. The public are
the important people.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.669
We need international observers;

00:17:35.669 --> 00:17:39.560
otherwise there is just going to be name-calling, so
we need a third party

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:44.640
that can certify whether the elections are going to 
be fair or not.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.080
CHANDA: President Musharraf has been criticized
recently,

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.510
severely, in the United States,

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:52.520
for not doing enough

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.320
to actually

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.190
capture the

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.780
Al-Qaeda suspects

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.210
hiding in Pakistan.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.000
What do you think of that? Do you think he is
doing enough?

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:05.560
BHUTTO: Well, I know that, as a Pakistani, it certainly
hurts me very much

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.050
when I see that inevitably the trail of terrorists
leads back to my country.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:13.790
If it's an issue of the Tube bomber,

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:19.650
we find that he had visited Pakistan, or
if it's an issue of John [Richard] Reed the shoe bomber, we

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:24.290
find that he had made a telephone call to Pakistan,
if it's capturing the CEO

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:28.169
of al-Qaeda, Khalid Sheikh, we find that he was
captured

00:18:28.169 --> 00:18:29.900
in Pakistan's garrison city

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:34.429
of Rawalpindi so it bothers us Pakistanis that 
our great nation

00:18:34.429 --> 00:18:38.720
should be associated with such elements. We
don't want to make our country

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.860
hospitable to such elements, and my party
severely criticized

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:46.160
the peace agreement that was signed in 2006

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:51.350
with the Taliban elements in the tribal 
regions of Pakistan,

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.180
and we feel that our tribal areas

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:56.750
were ceded to foreign elements: to Afghan Taliban

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.169
and Arab and Chechen militant fighters,

00:19:00.169 --> 00:19:04.980
and now those groups actually administer 
parts of our territory

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:11.180
and hold our people hostage. They dispense
their own form of justice; they teach little

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.360
twelve-year old boys to behead

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.730
those they accuse of being spies. I mean, little children
should have pens in their hands.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:22.200
Little children should have schools to go to.
Little children should have dreams.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.590
CHANDA: So why is it that

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:27.930
it can still continue in still Pakistani territory?

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.940
BHUTTO: Well, this is is a question that General Musharraf
and his regime must answer.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:35.410
While they have certainly verbally expressed their

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:39.250
sentiment for the right course of eliminating terrorism

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:42.750
and extremism in the country, unfortunately

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:46.920
they have not been able assert the rule of law
in the country.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.340
My government would move swiftly

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:51.690
to assert law and order

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.880
in the tribal areas of Pakistan,

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:58.480
to hunt down the al-Qaeda leaders who are
trying to take advantage of

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.000
the lack of law and order there,

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.929
to stop the drug trade, which is actually funding
and fueling terrorism,

00:20:04.929 --> 00:20:08.670
and to reform the political madrasahs, who use the
name "madrasah",

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:12.020
but are actually militant headquarters

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:16.370
using women and children as human shields.
I'm a woman; I'm a mother;

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:20.260
I don't want to see the innocent women and
children of my country

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:23.370
held up as human shields and killed

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:26.679
as they were during the Red Mosque Incident,

00:20:26.679 --> 00:20:29.210
and I think it's the duty of government

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:32.470
to provide the protection of the life and liberty

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:33.820
of its citizens.

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:36.170
CHANDA: So, given that fact that,

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.180
despite

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:41.700
President Musharraf's verbal assurances that
he's doing everything,

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:44.420
it is still continuing--in fact, increasing--

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:48.400
can you blame the Americans for saying they will

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.230
have to intervene without Pakistani permission?

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:54.990
BHUTTO: Well I can understand why they say that
because they feel that Islamabad has

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:55.600
failed

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:59.140
to stop the terrorists and that's why they
would like to move in,

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:01.220
but I would really urge against that.

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:05.320
I believe that the violation of
Pakistan's sovereignty

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.390
through unauthorized military action

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.029
will have very adverse consequences.

00:21:11.029 --> 00:21:16.000
When under attack, all Pakistanis will
forget their differences and they will all

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.990
unite, so any unauthorized action

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:23.760
would pit the NATO against all of the people
of Pakistan, and I don't think that's advisable.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.940
But I think what is advisable

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:30.980
is to have a close working relationship, and
certainly when the PPP is elected to power,

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:34.750
we intend to restore law and order 
to our tribal areas

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:38.400
and prevent the militants from attacking NATO,

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.360
so we intend to take away the causes

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:43.230
that can today threaten air strikes

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:46.690
against Pakistan, and we also intend to work
very closely

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:48.690
with NATO

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:51.320
and with the United States and other
countries

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:56.370
to eliminate terrorism, to help us also 
in our tribal areas,

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:00.940
to eliminate, through intelligence-sharing and
other means of cooperation.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:04.730
CHANDA: Pakistan has always sought a

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:08.110
strategic depth in Afghanistan as a part

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.540
of its security policy.

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:11.530
Do you think that

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:12.620
policy has

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:13.990
led to

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:17.370
this alliance, de facto alliance, between Pakistani

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:19.210
ISI and Taliban?

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:20.520
Can you change that?

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.150
BHUTTO: Well I certainly hope I can change it.

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:26.029
I believe that the policy of strategic depth

00:22:26.029 --> 00:22:27.740
has backfired,

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:30.809
and in fact it was in 1998

00:22:30.809 --> 00:22:34.170
that I stood up in the parliament of Pakistan
and I said

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:38.650
that the policy of strategic depth is turning
into one of strategic threat

00:22:38.650 --> 00:22:39.919
for Pakistan,

00:22:39.919 --> 00:22:42.350
and the passage of years have shown to me

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:47.559
that indeed such a policy is leading to militancy,
suicide bombers,

00:22:47.559 --> 00:22:50.180
weaponization, drug trade in Pakistan,

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:53.010
to an increase in poverty and unemployment

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:56.179
as the priorities of the state

00:22:56.179 --> 00:22:58.679
shift and these issues are neglected.

00:22:58.679 --> 00:23:03.119
So I want an end to that policy of strategic
depth. I think Afghanistan

00:23:03.119 --> 00:23:06.720
has traditionally been viewed either as a buffer state

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:11.730
or as a forward-policy state where there is
strategic depth,

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:14.250
and throughout history, different

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:17.630
empires, even the British empire

00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:22.040
or the Greeks when they even came to that
area, have looked at the issue in terms

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:24.160
of strategic depth or buffer state,

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:27.800
and I think for us it's much better to
have an Afghanistan

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.080
that is peaceful,

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:32.580
that allows us to trade with it, that has
good relations

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:37.180
with all its neighbors, and I think it's very
promising that Afghanistan has joined

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.420
the South Asian Association of Regional Countries,

00:23:40.420 --> 00:23:44.450
and I think for India, Pakistan, Afghanistan,
and the other countries of SAARC,

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:49.669
this is where we should concentrate. We should try to create
the economic interdependencies

00:23:49.669 --> 00:23:53.879
that allowed Europe to emerge from the
ravages of two world wars

00:23:53.879 --> 00:23:59.179
and build a common market that has given
unprecedented growth and an increase in the

00:23:59.179 --> 00:24:01.370
standard of living of ordinary Europeans.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:04.340
I mean, in the 50's people were all on rations,

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:07.800
and now they're spoiled for choice.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:10.510
CHANDA: Another issue where, I think,

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:13.100
you mentioned India--Kashmir--

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:15.790
seems to have been defused a little bit.

00:24:15.790 --> 00:24:19.940
Do you see any

00:24:19.940 --> 00:24:20.860
prospect that,

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:24.190
if you return to Pakistan as 
Prime Minister,

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:27.730
you will have a different approach than what has
been tried by Musharraf?

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:32.149
BHUTTO: No, I think Musharraf did the right thing
in following the spirit of the Simla Agreement

00:24:32.149 --> 00:24:36.110
which my father had signed with 
Prime Minister Indira Gandhi,

00:24:36.110 --> 00:24:40.610
and that the spirit of the declaration, 
the Islamabad declaration, wherein Rajiv Gandhi

00:24:40.610 --> 00:24:44.580
and I had decided to work for peaceful relations.

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:46.930
Certainly, the fighting over Kargil

00:24:46.930 --> 00:24:50.550
and the one million men who faced each
other eyeball-to-eyeball

00:24:50.550 --> 00:24:54.160
after the Indian parliament attack drove
home

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:59.230
the dramatic consequences of a conflict
between India and Pakistan, who are both nuclear-capable

00:24:59.230 --> 00:25:00.070
states.

00:25:00.070 --> 00:25:03.510
I don't think we can afford this; I think Musharraf
did the right thing.

00:25:03.510 --> 00:25:06.360
We've been very critical of him when he's done
the wrong thing,

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:11.670
but vis-à-vis the policy with India, or vis-à-vis,
the policy with women's rights,

00:25:11.670 --> 00:25:14.630
vis-à-vis restoring women's seats in parliament,

00:25:14.630 --> 00:25:18.010
well, we supported those measures because
we don't believe

00:25:18.010 --> 00:25:21.600
in being totally rejectionist or being totally

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:22.550
accepting.

00:25:22.550 --> 00:25:25.590
We believe in dealing with issue by issue.
So yes,

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:26.510
we would continue

00:25:26.510 --> 00:25:29.860
the process of dialogue with India.

00:25:29.860 --> 00:25:33.750
And not only that: I hope that in the 60th year 
of our anniversary

00:25:33.750 --> 00:25:36.360
(both countries are turning 60 in a few

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:37.660
day's time),

00:25:37.660 --> 00:25:41.710
I hope that we can come and build a peace
treaty

00:25:41.710 --> 00:25:44.860
that will enable our people to turn their 
backs

00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:48.180
on an unhappy past and look to a brighter future.

00:25:48.180 --> 00:25:51.179
Kashmir is an issue between us, it is
a dispute,

00:25:51.179 --> 00:25:53.910
but then you know, India has a dispute with
China

00:25:53.910 --> 00:25:56.700
over the border, but they don't go to war
with each other.

00:25:56.700 --> 00:26:00.830
So we need to learn that we can have
differing opinions

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:02.790
without actually allowing them

00:26:02.790 --> 00:26:09.530
to transform themselves into conflict, 
bloodshed, terrorism, militancy, or war.

00:26:09.530 --> 00:26:12.350
CHANDA: When you were Prime Minister,

00:26:12.350 --> 00:26:13.700
how much were you aware of

00:26:13.700 --> 00:26:14.940
A.Q. Khan's

00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:18.280
nuclear arms sales activities?

00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:22.380
BHUTTO: I was not at all aware of his 
nuclear arms sale

00:26:22.380 --> 00:26:23.130
opportunities.

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:28.630
In fact, as Prime Minister of Pakistan, my government
gave birth to the Benazir Nuclear Doctrine.

00:26:28.630 --> 00:26:30.920
Under this nuclear doctrine,

00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:36.000
Pakistan would not export nuclear technology--that
was a cardinal principle of the doctrine--

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:39.990
and we would not put together the 
components of a

00:26:39.990 --> 00:26:43.320
weapon unless our security was threatened,

00:26:43.320 --> 00:26:46.730
and then we would not shape and mold

00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:47.940
uranium into nuclear

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:49.720
parts.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:54.520
So it was a policy that was bipartisan; 
it came through with consultation with the

00:26:54.520 --> 00:26:56.240
presidency and the armed forces,

00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:59.990
so it was accepted by all as part of
the national interest,

00:26:59.990 --> 00:27:02.110
and, to my knowledge, it held

00:27:02.110 --> 00:27:04.919
until India detonated its nuclear devices,

00:27:04.919 --> 00:27:08.850
and then Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif in retaliation
detonated

00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:10.070
in Pakistan.

00:27:10.070 --> 00:27:12.520
So it was quite a shock that I learned

00:27:12.520 --> 00:27:16.130
that the no-export in nuclear technology had been
violated,

00:27:16.130 --> 00:27:20.169
and then I would not have believed it until 
A.Q. Khan came on television

00:27:20.169 --> 00:27:21.990
and confessed,

00:27:21.990 --> 00:27:26.410
and now the only question before us is, 
"Did he fall on his sword

00:27:26.410 --> 00:27:28.080
to protect others,

00:27:28.080 --> 00:27:30.340
or were there others also involved?"

00:27:30.340 --> 00:27:33.530
For that, my party called for a 
parliamentary inquiry,

00:27:33.530 --> 00:27:37.450
because Pakistan can't afford to 
endanger its own nuclear system

00:27:37.450 --> 00:27:39.739
by scientists who begin to smuggle

00:27:39.739 --> 00:27:41.190
and proliferate

00:27:41.190 --> 00:27:46.670
weapons of mass destruction.
CHANDA: But he was flying C1-30 of Pakistan Air Force

00:27:46.670 --> 00:27:47.580
to carry stuff,

00:27:47.580 --> 00:27:49.980
so is it possible that he was doing it alone?

00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:53.830
Well, this is the issue that we want resolved at the inquiry 
because it's amazing to

00:27:53.830 --> 00:27:55.410
think that he could have access

00:27:55.410 --> 00:27:59.149
to C1-30 aircraft and go to

00:27:59.149 --> 00:28:03.230
North Korea, and not only go to North Korea
but go to so many

00:28:03.230 --> 00:28:06.680
other countries. I remember in 
General Musharraf's regime

00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:11.440
there had been a full-page advertisement taken out 
by the Ministry of Commerce

00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:14.940
advertising the sale of nuclear components,
and many of us were shocked.

00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:18.660
This was before A.Q. Khan's whole issue had been

00:28:18.660 --> 00:28:20.380
unearthed.

00:28:20.380 --> 00:28:26.780
So it was actually very shocking and particularly
in this world in which we live,

00:28:26.780 --> 00:28:29.740
you know, where terrorists want to get their hands

00:28:29.740 --> 00:28:31.960
on weapons of mass destruction.

00:28:31.960 --> 00:28:37.020
The entire world community, including Pakistanis
who live in the diaspora, as well as

00:28:37.020 --> 00:28:40.610
all other human beings could face devastating
consequences

00:28:40.610 --> 00:28:42.320
if

00:28:42.320 --> 00:28:43.919
mad people

00:28:43.919 --> 00:28:45.420
manage to get lured by money.

00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:48.720
So I'd really like to find out more

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:51.500
about how A.Q. Khan went around

00:28:51.500 --> 00:28:53.950
doing this. Musharraf has pardoned him;

00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:54.980
well, that's

00:28:54.980 --> 00:28:56.510
one end of the spectrum

00:28:56.510 --> 00:29:00.380
but the other end of the spectrum is: we must make sure that
something like this can never

00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:02.980
happen again.

00:29:02.980 --> 00:29:05.080
CHANDA: Had A.Q. Khan

00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:06.300
not engaged in these kind

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:07.809
of activities,

00:29:07.809 --> 00:29:12.410
would it have been possible today for 
Pakistan to sign a civilian nuclear agreement

00:29:12.410 --> 00:29:15.030
with the United States as India has done?

00:29:15.030 --> 00:29:17.170
BHUTTO: It's a difficult call,

00:29:17.170 --> 00:29:18.460
it's a difficult call.

00:29:18.460 --> 00:29:22.169
I think that India's a larger market,

00:29:22.169 --> 00:29:25.169
and India is five times larger than Pakistan,

00:29:25.169 --> 00:29:29.950
and certainly the post-Cold War, many academics
had predicted

00:29:29.950 --> 00:29:34.710
that the Western world would
start coming closer to India,

00:29:34.710 --> 00:29:39.040
so it's difficult to call, but certainly Pakistanis are 
disappointed that we weren't

00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:40.220
offered the same

00:29:40.220 --> 00:29:42.600
civil nuclear

00:29:42.600 --> 00:29:43.070
agreement.

00:29:43.070 --> 00:29:48.890
I hope that at some stage we are able to
be offered such a civil nuclear cooperation,

00:29:48.890 --> 00:29:54.919
but I also want to take my generation away
from the earlier generation's view

00:29:54.919 --> 00:29:59.590
of tit-for-tat with India. I mean, we can't keep
competing with the Joneses.

00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:02.970
We have to identify our own core

00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:03.540
interests.

00:30:03.540 --> 00:30:08.580
We need to pursue our core interests

00:30:08.580 --> 00:30:12.340
and not seek to so overextend ourselves that we begin to 
collapse from within, and I think that's what the policy of

00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:13.580
strategic depth has done.

00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:14.570
It's threatening

00:30:14.570 --> 00:30:16.159
Pakistan from within,

00:30:16.159 --> 00:30:17.930
and today, if I risk my life

00:30:17.930 --> 00:30:19.460
to go back to my country,

00:30:19.460 --> 00:30:22.150
I do it because I see the threat within

00:30:22.150 --> 00:30:24.300
and I want to try and help my people

00:30:24.300 --> 00:30:27.400
and help my country avert disaster.

00:30:27.400 --> 00:30:30.390
CHANDA: The last question--if General

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:31.360
Musharraf

00:30:31.360 --> 00:30:35.970
does not

00:30:35.970 --> 00:30:38.970
doff his military uniform,

00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:42.100
would you still go back to Pakistan before 
the end of the year?

00:30:42.100 --> 00:30:46.930
Yes, I will go back to Pakistan whether Musharraf
takes his uniform off or not.

00:30:46.930 --> 00:30:49.700
I will go back to Pakistan this year

00:30:49.700 --> 00:30:52.870
irrespective of whether we have an agreement
with General Musharraf or not,

00:30:52.870 --> 00:30:55.890
but I hope that General Musharraf will review,

00:30:55.890 --> 00:31:01.100
in light of the circumstances in Pakistan,
after the restoration of the Chief Justice of Pakistan,

00:31:01.100 --> 00:31:06.100
his decision to seek reelection in uniform
from the present assemblies.

00:31:06.100 --> 00:31:07.150
CHANDA: Thank you very much,

00:31:07.150 --> 00:31:08.580
Mrs. Bhutto.

00:31:08.580 --> 00:31:08.830
BHUTTO: Thank you. Thank you very much.

